  "rationale": "Both answers are understandable and valid, but the national split is materially overstated. Indonesian and Malaysian usage permits substantial overlap: pekerja is a general employee term in Malaysian Malay, karyawan means an employee/worker in Indonesian, and Malay dictionaries treat panduan and pedoman as overlapping guide/handbook terms. Indonesian official usage also includes Buku Panduan Pekerja. The different-common-word relation is therefore not defensible as a strong variety distinction. The blank contrast should also be populated or the relation removed; no genuine false-friend contrast is established.",
